    <updated>2026-09-24T06:00:00Z</updated>
    <author><name>AATF AI News Aggregator</name></author>
    <summary type="html"><![CDATA[<p><strong>Bot Screen / Desktop Passthrough Launch (dominant story):</strong> <strong>@NousResearch</strong> unveiled <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-ef6b4179c4fa" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bot Screen</a></strong> in <strong>Hermes Desktop</strong>, live-streaming any bot session — browser driving, terminal typing, window use — to massive engagement (1958 likes, 394k views). Founder <strong>@Teknium</strong> followed with the interactive companion announcement: users can now <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-4784626f2a61" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">visually and interactively access the same machine</a> as their <strong>Hermes Agent</strong> via remote gateways (1141 likes, 173k views). Official documentation and a <strong>@tonbistudio</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d84a2bc0a85d" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">walkthrough video</a> (540 likes) round out the launch, and community hype ran hot — '<a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-014ad26a44c6" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Finally!</a>', '<a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-48968e1c836e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Much needed!</a>', '<a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-015fe011793b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Impressive!</a>'. <strong>Community OSS / oh-my-hermes Ecosystem:</strong> Prioritized community author <strong>@rlaope</strong> had a prolific stretch, <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-99948938337f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">open-sourcing <strong>jeval</strong></a> (JEV evaluation with visual result extraction) and shipping a <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-415aecf318f8" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">major <strong>oh-my-hermes (OMH)</strong> update</a> adding <strong>Jev-Skils</strong>, model aliases, and routing across skills/models/agents/memory/<strong>MCP</strong> — signaling a fast-maturing <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-b4d141253a4f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">community plugin layer around <strong>hermes-agent</strong></a>. <strong>Guides &amp; Usage Tips:</strong> <strong>@Teknium</strong> amplified <strong>@tonbistudio</strong>'s <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d03d44ef66a9" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">guide video</a>, and <strong>@NousResearch</strong> shared a practical tip: <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-768697783517" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">run <strong>Hermes via iMessage</strong></a> with whichever model you prefer. <strong>Maintainer Engagement &amp; Sentiment:</strong> The overall mood is excitement plus confidence in responsiveness — <strong>@Teknium</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d5a2f794eeec" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">pushed back on an unverified cache-bug claim</a> with clear repro-issue guidance, <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-992950038a21" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">clarified a misattributed project</a> as built by <strong>NousResearch</strong> rather than <strong>Anthropic</strong>, and <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-3e1742f36c0b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">confirmed a same-day fix</a> after user feedback. Sentiment skews strongly positive, with <strong>@rlaope</strong> also musing that <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-797e0ee6c95e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Opus 5.5</strong> is impressive but voicing hesitation on <strong>Claude Code</strong></a> — implicitly positioning <strong>Hermes Agent</strong> as the community alternative.</p>]]></summary>
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p><strong>Bot Screen / Desktop Passthrough Launch (dominant story):</strong> <strong>@NousResearch</strong> unveiled <strong><a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-ef6b4179c4fa" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bot Screen</a></strong> in <strong>Hermes Desktop</strong>, live-streaming any bot session — browser driving, terminal typing, window use — to massive engagement (1958 likes, 394k views). Founder <strong>@Teknium</strong> followed with the interactive companion announcement: users can now <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-4784626f2a61" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">visually and interactively access the same machine</a> as their <strong>Hermes Agent</strong> via remote gateways (1141 likes, 173k views). Official documentation and a <strong>@tonbistudio</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d84a2bc0a85d" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">walkthrough video</a> (540 likes) round out the launch, and community hype ran hot — '<a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-014ad26a44c6" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Finally!</a>', '<a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-48968e1c836e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Much needed!</a>', '<a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-015fe011793b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">Impressive!</a>'. <strong>Community OSS / oh-my-hermes Ecosystem:</strong> Prioritized community author <strong>@rlaope</strong> had a prolific stretch, <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-99948938337f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">open-sourcing <strong>jeval</strong></a> (JEV evaluation with visual result extraction) and shipping a <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-415aecf318f8" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">major <strong>oh-my-hermes (OMH)</strong> update</a> adding <strong>Jev-Skils</strong>, model aliases, and routing across skills/models/agents/memory/<strong>MCP</strong> — signaling a fast-maturing <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-b4d141253a4f" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">community plugin layer around <strong>hermes-agent</strong></a>. <strong>Guides &amp; Usage Tips:</strong> <strong>@Teknium</strong> amplified <strong>@tonbistudio</strong>'s <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d03d44ef66a9" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">guide video</a>, and <strong>@NousResearch</strong> shared a practical tip: <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-768697783517" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">run <strong>Hermes via iMessage</strong></a> with whichever model you prefer. <strong>Maintainer Engagement &amp; Sentiment:</strong> The overall mood is excitement plus confidence in responsiveness — <strong>@Teknium</strong> <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-d5a2f794eeec" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">pushed back on an unverified cache-bug claim</a> with clear repro-issue guidance, <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-992950038a21" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">clarified a misattributed project</a> as built by <strong>NousResearch</strong> rather than <strong>Anthropic</strong>, and <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-3e1742f36c0b" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer">confirmed a same-day fix</a> after user feedback. Sentiment skews strongly positive, with <strong>@rlaope</strong> also musing that <a href="https://hermes-agent-news.vercel.app/?date=2026-09-24&amp;category=social#item-797e0ee6c95e" class="internal-link" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Opus 5.5</strong> is impressive but voicing hesitation on <strong>Claude Code</strong></a> — implicitly positioning <strong>Hermes Agent</strong> as the community alternative.</p>]]></content>
